The regeneration timing window is defined as:
\[
T_{\text{reg}} = \tau_0 \cdot f\big(\mathcal{E}_{\text{stress}}(t)\big),
\]
where $f$ is a monotonic scaling function. A damping coefficient
$\sigma_{\text{threshold}}$ suppresses runaway activation:
\[
\sigma_{\text{threshold}} = g\big(\mathcal{E}_{\text{stress}}(t)\big).
\]

\section{Cell-Cycle Invariant System}
Define the invariant functional:
\[
\mathcal{I}_{\text{cc}} = F\big(n, \mathcal{K}_{\text{DNA}}, \mathbf{J}_{\text{biochem}}\big),
